+n := parse-input(@args/count, @args/1)
+```
+
+This accepts one payload argument and rejects extra arguments. Missing arguments
+and invalid Unicode remain checked resource errors. An empty single argument
+counts as one and then fails the strict numeric parser. Failed source turns do
+not deliver staged terminal output. Resource acquisition can precede the pure
+pattern check, so this does not promise arity errors before all resource errors.
+Ordinary match expressions still require exhaustive coverage.
